<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply rises in November.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply rises in November.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$1.49 billion to C$67.19 billion in November from C$65.70 billion in October and compared with C$59.83 billion in November 1995, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   Nov 96     Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p>M1					 67.19	65.70	59.83</p>
<p>M2					396.29     393.68     385.18</p>
<p>M3					497.23     492.77     470.73</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Nov	   Oct</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-13.40	-12.97</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     672.34	658.20</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    109,16	104.58</p>
<p>				    Wk to Dec 18  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  28.215  +0.675     +0.244</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     6.570  +1.279     -2.604</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	464.897  +0.379     +6.468</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 137.600  -2.600    -24.700</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.474  -0.021     +2.008</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
